<section class="cmp-main-section" aria-labelledby="faq-section">
  <div class="wrapper wrapper--960 wrapper--mobile-38 wrapper--tablet-48">

    <div class="cmp-header-text-container" data-animate="fade-in">
      <span class="cmp-topper-heading">COMMON QUESTIONS</span>
      <h2 id="faq-section" class="cmp-main-heading">Asked and <span class="cmp-heading-span cmp-gradient-text">answered.</span></h2>
    </div>

    <div data-animate="slide-right">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <button>
          Why is it so much cheaper than an agency?
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M9 9L15 15M15 9L9 15M21 12C21 16.9706 16.9706 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 7.02944 7.02944 3 12 3C16.9706 3 21 7.02944 21 12Z" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <div class="faq-item__answer">
          <p>Because there simply is no agency involved. It’s just me and a designer working directly with you from start to finish. That means no account managers, project managers, or layers of overhead adding to the cost. You are paying for the website itself and the expertise behind it, not the extra expenses that come with a traditional agency.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button>
          What does "unlimited edits" actually cover?
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M9 9L15 15M15 9L9 15M21 12C21 16.9706 16.9706 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 7.02944 7.02944 3 12 3C16.9706 3 21 7.02944 21 12Z" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <div class="faq-item__answer">
          <p>This covers all the small changes you will need to keep your website up to date. That includes things like updating text, changing menu items, adding or replacing images, updating contact details, or making other minor content changes. <br><br> If you ever need something larger, such as adding a new section, creating a new page, or making major design or functionality changes, there may be a small additional charge depending on the amount of work involved. If that is ever the case, I'll always discuss it with you and agree on the price before any work begins, there will never be any surprise costs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button>
          Are there any hidden costs?
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M9 9L15 15M15 9L9 15M21 12C21 16.9706 16.9706 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 7.02944 7.02944 3 12 3C16.9706 3 21 7.02944 21 12Z" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <div class="faq-item__answer">
          <p>No. I believe in being completely transparent about pricing, so you will never be surprised by any hidden fees or unexpected charges. If you ever request work that falls outside what is included in your plan, I'll explain exactly what is involved, provide the fixed price in advance and only go ahead once you have approved everything in writing. You will always know exactly what you are paying for before any additional work begins.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button>
          Do I own the website?
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M9 9L15 15M15 9L9 15M21 12C21 16.9706 16.9706 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 7.02944 7.02944 3 12 3C16.9706 3 21 7.02944 21 12Z" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <div class="faq-item__answer">
          <p>It depends on the plan you choose. With the one-time build, you own the website and all of its source code and free to do with it as you please. Once the project is complete, you can host it wherever you like, make changes yourself, or work with another developer in the future. <br><br> With the monthly plan, the source code remains mine. This allows me to provide ongoing hosting, maintenance, updates, and support as part of the service while keeping the monthly cost affordable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button>
          What happens if I want to leave?
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M9 9L15 15M15 9L9 15M21 12C21 16.9706 16.9706 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 7.02944 7.02944 3 12 3C16.9706 3 21 7.02944 21 12Z" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <div class="faq-item__answer">
          <p>That depends on which plan you're on. If you chose the one-time build, you are free to cancel any ongoing support or maintenance services whenever you like. Since you own the website, you are free to continue managing it yourself or work with another developer if you prefer. <br><br> If you are on the monthly plan, there is a minimum commitment of a six month contract. After that, you can cancel at any time with no penalties or hidden fees at all.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button>
          Can i cancel after the six months and still keep the website?
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path d="M9 9L15 15M15 9L9 15M21 12C21 16.9706 16.9706 21 12 21C7.02944 21 3 16.9706 3 12C3 7.02944 7.02944 3 12 3C16.9706 3 21 7.02944 21 12Z" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
          </svg>
        </button>

        <div class="faq-item__answer">
          <p>No. With the monthly plan, the website remains part of the ongoing service, so if you cancel your subscription, the website and its source code are not transferred to you. <br><br> The monthly plan is designed to provide an affordable way to have a professional website without the large upfront cost of a one-time build. If owning the website outright is important to you, the one-time build is the better option, as you will own the website and its source code once the project is complete. <br><br> For many small businesses, however, what matters most is having a fast, professional website that is looked after for them, rather than owning the underlying source code. The monthly plan is designed with exactly that in mind.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

